<p>The Pentagon is drafting options for possible US ground operations in Iran that could last for weeks, according to multiple reports. The missions under discussion would stop short of a full-scale invasion and instead lean on Special Operations forces and conventional infantry. Options include seizing Kharg Island and carrying out raids near the Strait of Hormuz to destroy weapons that threaten shipping. Whether President Trump will approve any of those plans remains unclear.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/39RtjHeN1wmKteIwagYOXUP_nQBwDiJEWYCO5YVUkdZdrGAsW9eEdvot8vA6PyqXbt4HyOux_6B2NG7sC_D0b9rrIpqFpENzePWtxUvK20oiWSs4VI1kaCdikooK103UI6cTbWrvFOaW6m3WglfcogfYN9MkNxX1mUSwGNrgqOZcdkEN9RPZLnNkNg' alt='Image published with reporting on possible US ground operations in Iran' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Operational framing: The reports pointed to something more sustained than a one-off strike, which helps explain why staging, lift, and offshore support matter here.</li><li>Force posture: RT said the USS Tripoli brought about 3,500 sailors and Marines, along with transport aircraft, strike aircraft, and amphibious assault assets, into the broader regional picture.</li><li>Additional ships: RT also said another amphibious ready group built around the USS Boxer, alongside USS Comstock and USS Portland, was moving toward the region.</li><li>Source trail: The Washington Post accounts, as cited in later reports, relied on unnamed US officials, which means the planning surfaced anonymously rather than through a formal public announcement.</li></ul><blockquote>Maximum optionality - Karoline Leavitt</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Pentagon planners: Officials described a range of options centered on raids by Special Operations forces and conventional infantry, defining the ground concept by unit type and mission scale rather than by massed force. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/pentagon-preparing-for-ground-operations-in-iran-reports-us-media/article70798609.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>White House: Press secretary Karoline Leavitt said the Pentagon&#x27;s role is to give the commander-in-chief &quot;maximum optionality,&quot; framing the work as a menu of contingencies rather than a public decision. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/636595-us-plans-ground-raids-iran/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Washington Post reporting as relayed by Reuters: The planning reportedly looked at an extended run of operations rather than a one-night mission, suggesting attention to campaign design as well as the decision to escalate. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/pentagon-preparing-weeks-ground-operations-iran-washington-post-reports'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/pentagon-preparing-weeks-ground-operations-iran-washington-post-reports'>Pentagon preparing for weeks of ground operations in Iran, Washington Post reports</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/iran-us-war-raids-near-strait-hormuz-seizure-of-kharg-island-trump-prepares-for-weeks-of-ground-ops-in-iran-11280850#publisher=newsstand'>Raids Near Hormuz, Seizing Kharg: US Prepares For Weeks Of Ground Ops In Iran</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/pentagon-preparing-for-ground-operations-in-iran-reports-us-media/article70798609.ece'>Pentagon preparing for ground operations in Iran, reports U.S. media</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/636595-us-plans-ground-raids-iran/'>US prepares for ‘weeks‘ of ground raids in Iran – WaPo</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1s6kayx/pentagon_prepares_for_weeks_of_ground_operations/'>Pentagon prepares for weeks of ground operations in Iran</a> - reddit.com</li></ul>